WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.968
-This is familiar.
I like this seat.

00:00:02.968 --> 00:00:05.033
-Yeah, you do.
The last time you were here,

00:00:05.033 --> 00:00:06.801
it was after your final game.
-Yeah.

00:00:06.801 --> 00:00:08.100
-Do you remember
when you were here?

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.067
You remember what was happening?
-It's a little foggy.

00:00:10.067 --> 00:00:12.501
-Yeah, because you were --
-I had a hangover.

00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:14.033
-Yeah.

00:00:14.033 --> 00:00:16.300
-I had my first hangover.
-Exactly right.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:18.200
-But I was wondering
once I left,

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:21.367
why was there a nurse right
there in the room when I --

00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:23.667
I'll just leave that alone.

00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:25.501
I never been somewhere where
they had a nurse right away.

00:00:25.501 --> 00:00:27.501
-Yeah, we took care of you, man.
-I was like, "I got a hangover."

00:00:27.501 --> 00:00:30.100
The nurse came out of nowhere.
-Because you don't drink, right?

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:31.734
You're an athlete.
-Well, yeah, I drink.

00:00:31.734 --> 00:00:33.567
-You drink,
yeah, but not that much.

00:00:33.567 --> 00:00:36.234
-No, I drink a lot.
-You do?

00:00:36.234 --> 00:00:37.767
-I have my own wine.

00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:39.734
-I know you do now,
but, I mean --

00:00:39.734 --> 00:00:42.300
-Well, I never got drunk
like that.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:45.000
Like, I've always been able to
be, like, cut off.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:46.300
It's time to go.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:49.701
But that night, after my
last game of my entire career,

00:00:49.701 --> 00:00:51.467
I was, like, to the wall.

00:00:51.467 --> 00:00:53.200
-Yeah. You went for it.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:54.534
And then you were like,

00:00:54.534 --> 00:00:55.667
"Jimmy, I hope I'm okay.

00:00:55.667 --> 00:00:57.734
I'm sorry if I'm going to be
a little foggy."

00:00:57.734 --> 00:00:58.834
You were fantastic.

00:00:58.834 --> 00:00:59.934
-I was?
-Yes.

00:00:59.934 --> 00:01:01.234
-Don't remember.
-Alright. Good.

00:01:01.234 --> 00:01:02.934
Don't have to remember.
Don't worry about it.

00:01:02.934 --> 00:01:05.067
You've been very busy in
your retirement, by the way.

00:01:05.067 --> 00:01:07.434
You wrote a memoir.
You have fashion brands.

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:08.968
You have a wine, you just said.

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:11.801
And no big deal -- you bought
a piece of an NBA team.

00:01:11.801 --> 00:01:14.133
You're part owner of
the Utah Jazz.

00:01:14.133 --> 00:01:17.200
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you. Thank you.

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:20.334
-How -- Couple questions there.

00:01:20.334 --> 00:01:23.167
How did you get involved
with Utah Jazz?

00:01:23.167 --> 00:01:25.133
And how did that end up being?

00:01:25.133 --> 00:01:27.767
-Ryan Smith,
who's the owner of the Jazz,

00:01:27.767 --> 00:01:29.200
very good friend of mine

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:33.267
and around the same age --
41 years old.

00:01:33.267 --> 00:01:36.701
And, so, playing golf, as well.
We golf together.

00:01:36.701 --> 00:01:38.701
Talked about doing
business together one day.

00:01:38.701 --> 00:01:42.200
And he one day bought a team
called the Utah Jazz,

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.734
flew to my house,
and asked me to be a part of it.

00:01:44.734 --> 00:01:46.267
-I love the name Utah Jazz.

00:01:46.267 --> 00:01:48.634
Robert, how's the
jazz scene in Utah?

00:01:48.634 --> 00:01:50.934
-Does not exist.
-Exactly.

00:01:50.934 --> 00:01:53.100
-All-Star Weekend
is in Utah this year.

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:54.300
What's up?
-Oh, I'm down.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:55.701
-Talk to me.
-Oh, yeah, you know Robert.

00:01:55.701 --> 00:01:57.467
-You know what I'm saying?
-I'll bring jazz to Utah.

00:01:57.467 --> 00:01:58.767
-That's what I'm talking about.
Let's do it.

00:01:58.767 --> 00:02:00.434
-That's the way it works.
-Let's do it.

00:02:00.434 --> 00:02:01.834
-That's the way it works.
-Yeah.

00:02:01.834 --> 00:02:04.167
-Does it get frustrating
for you, as an owner of a team,

00:02:04.167 --> 00:02:05.567
to watch the players,
and you're like,

00:02:05.567 --> 00:02:06.901
"I don't know
if I can watch them."

00:02:06.901 --> 00:02:09.133
Because you know how to do it.
-Yeah, see? It's hard.

00:02:09.133 --> 00:02:10.167
-It is, right?

00:02:10.167 --> 00:02:11.767
-It's hard watching
a game period.

00:02:11.767 --> 00:02:12.767
-Yeah, cause you want to
get in there and go,

00:02:12.767 --> 00:02:13.868
"No, I'll show you how to do it.

00:02:13.868 --> 00:02:14.934
You do this and then that
and then this."

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:15.968
-Because all
you're thinking about is

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:17.534
what you would do, right?

00:02:17.534 --> 00:02:19.634
Like, you hoop a lot,
as I've heard.

00:02:19.634 --> 00:02:21.033
-Yes.
-Right?

00:02:21.033 --> 00:02:24.334
Do you think about what you
would do when you watch the NBA?

00:02:24.334 --> 00:02:28.467
-Well, I think,
"Wow, I'd like to do that."

00:02:28.467 --> 00:02:30.400
Are y'all rebuilding?

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:31.734
-We're reshaping.

00:02:31.734 --> 00:02:33.267
-Yeah, reshaping.

00:02:33.267 --> 00:02:34.801
-We don't use "rebuild"
in the NBA.

00:02:34.801 --> 00:02:36.000
-Nice terminology.
-Reshaping.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.234
-Reshaping.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, I like that.

00:02:38.234 --> 00:02:40.434
You've played basketball,
pickup, with some of

00:02:40.434 --> 00:02:41.968
the biggest celebrities around.

00:02:41.968 --> 00:02:45.434
I have a picture of you
playing with Adam Sandler.

00:02:45.434 --> 00:02:46.667
How's Adam's game?

00:02:46.667 --> 00:02:48.601
-Adam's nice.

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:52.667
So, that was 2006, the day after
I won my first championship.

00:02:52.667 --> 00:02:55.434
-No big deal.
-No big deal. Thank you.

00:02:55.434 --> 00:02:58.200
And I got the chance to spend
some time with him in the back,

00:02:58.200 --> 00:02:59.934
and he told me that,
at the time,

00:02:59.934 --> 00:03:03.234
they called him
"The White Dwyane Wade,"

00:03:03.234 --> 00:03:05.434
because I was really known for

00:03:05.434 --> 00:03:06.934
my backboard shots around
that time.

00:03:06.934 --> 00:03:08.467
I would come down
and shoot off the glass.

00:03:08.467 --> 00:03:10.801
And Adam got a little
two-hand backboard shot.

00:03:10.801 --> 00:03:13.000
And so they was calling him
The White D-Wade.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:14.200
-Is that right?
-Yeah.

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:16.868
-I've got to ask him about that.
How about this?

00:03:16.868 --> 00:03:18.033
With President Obama.

00:03:18.033 --> 00:03:20.834
You played a pickup game
with President Obama.

00:03:20.834 --> 00:03:23.734
How is his game, first of all?
-Yeah.

00:03:23.734 --> 00:03:26.400
So, legendary. Legendary.
-It is, right?

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.567
-I played a pickup game
with President Obama

00:03:28.567 --> 00:03:31.567
on his 49th birthday.

00:03:31.567 --> 00:03:34.501
It was, like, a cryptic e-mail
that came through.

00:03:34.501 --> 00:03:35.834
I didn't really know
if I was, like --

00:03:35.834 --> 00:03:37.467
if I was just showing up

00:03:37.467 --> 00:03:39.000
and then somebody
was playing a trick on me

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:40.868
or was it actually,
like, president's birthday

00:03:40.868 --> 00:03:42.000
and we were going to hoop.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:43.734
-At The White House.
-At The White House.

00:03:43.734 --> 00:03:45.033
All it said was,

00:03:45.033 --> 00:03:47.567
"Show up to The White House
and bring your sneakers."

00:03:47.567 --> 00:03:49.267
And I was like, "I'm going."

00:03:49.267 --> 00:03:53.067
I don't know who this is from,
but I'm showing up.

00:03:53.067 --> 00:03:56.000
But -- He's actually --
He's not bad.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.400
-Really?
-He's a lefty.

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:59.467
He has a real --
As smooth as he is,

00:03:59.467 --> 00:04:00.667
that's how smooth his game is.

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:01.968
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:04:01.968 --> 00:04:03.901
-How's Trump's game?
-Who?

00:04:03.901 --> 00:04:05.601
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.601 --> 00:04:07.734
[ Cymbal crash ]

00:04:07.734 --> 00:04:11.434
-He said, "Who?" He said, "Who?"

00:04:11.434 --> 00:04:13.634
-Didn't get that e-mail, huh?
-No, I didn't get that one.

00:04:13.634 --> 00:04:14.767
-Yeah.

00:04:14.767 --> 00:04:18.934
-So, we're scrimmaging with
President Obama,

00:04:18.934 --> 00:04:20.834
and he brings us all in
and he'd say,

00:04:20.834 --> 00:04:22.200
"Hey, I want you guys
to play hard

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:24.300
and play like
this is a real game."

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:25.601
And then
we looked around the court,

00:04:25.601 --> 00:04:28.234
and there's Secret Service
all around the court.

00:04:28.234 --> 00:04:30.334
And it's like,
"We can't touch you."

00:04:30.334 --> 00:04:31.968
-We can't play a real game.
What are you talking about?

00:04:31.968 --> 00:04:34.067
-We can't foul you for real.

00:04:34.067 --> 00:04:35.901
-Imagine if you did that?
-No, Joakim Noah did.

00:04:35.901 --> 00:04:37.033
-He did?

00:04:37.033 --> 00:04:38.334
-Oh, he picked him up
full court,

00:04:38.334 --> 00:04:39.534
was elbowing him,
and everything.

00:04:39.534 --> 00:04:40.634
It was great.
-As you should.

00:04:40.634 --> 00:04:42.200
-That's why he
never got invited back.

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:43.767
-Yo, you would [bleep] Biden.

00:04:43.767 --> 00:04:45.601
-Alright, alright.

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:49.801
Let's not get any ideas.
That's not going to go down.

00:04:49.801 --> 00:04:52.601
We actually...
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.601 --> 00:04:54.834
Joe, do not invite --
I don't want to see this happen.

00:04:54.834 --> 00:04:56.167
Please.

00:04:56.167 --> 00:04:59.300
There's another player
I'd like to get your take on.

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:00.734
I'm curious if you think
he's any good.

00:05:00.734 --> 00:05:03.367
He played in the NBA Celebrity
Game earlier this year.

00:05:03.367 --> 00:05:05.634
We have a clip.
Take a look at this guy.

00:05:05.634 --> 00:05:07.701
-You know what it is, guys?
I was just --

00:05:07.701 --> 00:05:09.767
-Uh-oh.
-Back again.

00:05:09.767 --> 00:05:11.701
-Make the extra pass.

00:05:11.701 --> 00:05:12.834
-Oh!

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:17.334
-Oh!

00:05:17.334 --> 00:05:20.000
-Where'd that guy come from?

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.634
-So, initially --
Let me see this shot.

00:05:21.634 --> 00:05:23.667
-What are you seeing out of
Jack Harlow here?

00:05:23.667 --> 00:05:27.300
-I see him turning --
-Shawn Marion influence.

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:29.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:29.033 --> 00:05:31.033
-Shawn Marion?
That's what I was thinking.

00:05:31.033 --> 00:05:32.467
-What were you thinking?
-Shawn Marion.

00:05:32.467 --> 00:05:34.367
He shoots like --
Shout-out to Shawn Marion.

00:05:34.367 --> 00:05:36.067
-From, like, the pelvis --
-Yeah.

00:05:36.067 --> 00:05:37.501
You shoot like the ball was hot.

00:05:37.501 --> 00:05:39.000
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:40.367
Like, he laid it up like it was
like a hot plate in his hand.

00:05:40.367 --> 00:05:42.200
He was like...

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:44.367
-Well, sometimes,
that's when the lights are on.

00:05:44.367 --> 00:05:48.100
You know, your form
changes under pressure.

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:49.501
But it's been
restructured since.

00:05:49.501 --> 00:05:50.701
-It's been restructured?
-Yeah.

00:05:50.701 --> 00:05:53.234
-It went in. It looks --

00:05:53.234 --> 00:05:55.601
-Did you like the clips?
What did you think of the clips?

00:05:55.601 --> 00:05:57.434
-It looks terrible.
-Oh.

00:05:57.434 --> 00:05:59.067
But it's effective.

00:05:59.067 --> 00:06:00.868
-You're lucky we don't have your
highlights up here.

00:06:00.868 --> 00:06:02.567
-Well, I mean, I wish you did.

00:06:02.567 --> 00:06:04.300
I'm play them for my son
all the time and like,

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:05.300
"Look at your dad."

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:08.300
-Yeah, watch what dad -- Yeah.

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:09.801
Let's talk about
"The Redeem Team."

00:06:09.801 --> 00:06:11.334
-Yes, sir.
-Congrats on this.

00:06:11.334 --> 00:06:13.300
Thanks for doing this,
executive-producing this.

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:14.968
But explain to people
if they don't know what

00:06:14.968 --> 00:06:16.567
"The Redeem Team" was, can you?

00:06:16.567 --> 00:06:23.067
-Yes. So, 2004,
the Olympics in Athens, Greece,

00:06:23.067 --> 00:06:25.968
which it was a tough time
in the world around that time.

00:06:25.968 --> 00:06:27.801
A lot of the stars players
in the NBA

00:06:27.801 --> 00:06:30.467
were opting out of playing
in the Olympics

00:06:30.467 --> 00:06:33.734
because of war things going on
in the world.

00:06:33.734 --> 00:06:35.434
And so they called on
the younger guys --

00:06:35.434 --> 00:06:38.501
myself, Carmelo, LeBron --
to join this team.

00:06:38.501 --> 00:06:41.267
And we joined this team with
Allen Iverson, Tim Duncan,

00:06:41.267 --> 00:06:43.133
Stephon Marbury,
and all these great,

00:06:43.133 --> 00:06:44.467
you know, NBA players.

00:06:44.467 --> 00:06:46.033
And, so, we were like, "Cool.

00:06:46.033 --> 00:06:48.767
We're about to go win us
a gold medal."

00:06:48.767 --> 00:06:50.067
And that didn't happen.

00:06:50.067 --> 00:06:52.200
We won the bronze.

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:55.367
We were pretty terrible
as a team.

00:06:55.367 --> 00:06:58.601
-Worst summer of my life, bro.
-Yeah, it was...

00:06:58.601 --> 00:07:00.100
-Worst summer of his life.

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:04.667
It really bummed him out.
But, I mean, that was -- Yeah.

00:07:04.667 --> 00:07:06.868
-Well, I mean, I think,
at the time, we realized, one,

00:07:06.868 --> 00:07:10.267
that the world,
like, was not catching up --

00:07:10.267 --> 00:07:11.501
they had caught up, right?

00:07:11.501 --> 00:07:12.734
We were playing
against teams that had been

00:07:12.734 --> 00:07:14.567
playing together since
they were 16 years old,

00:07:14.567 --> 00:07:15.767
maybe even younger.

00:07:15.767 --> 00:07:18.501
And so the chemistry that
they had we did not have.

00:07:18.501 --> 00:07:21.400
We got together two weeks before
in Jacksonville.

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:23.067
-And you're own stars
in your own rights,

00:07:23.067 --> 00:07:25.400
so you're like, "I don't really
know how to play as a team

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:26.634
with these guys,
'cause --" Yeah.

00:07:26.634 --> 00:07:28.467
-And then, it's the rules.
It's FIBA rules.

00:07:28.467 --> 00:07:29.601
It's a FIBA game.

00:07:29.601 --> 00:07:31.267
You got to learn
how to play their game.

00:07:31.267 --> 00:07:33.033
It's not the NBA game.

00:07:33.033 --> 00:07:35.834
The rules are different.
And, so, the ball is different.

00:07:35.834 --> 00:07:37.000
Everything is different.

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:39.400
And, so, we got together,
and, like, it was --

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:41.868
The practice was a tragedy.
-It was just --

00:07:41.868 --> 00:07:43.601
-It was a separation between
teams, too.

00:07:43.601 --> 00:07:45.767
Like, it was just
a thrown-together team.

00:07:45.767 --> 00:07:48.667
And, so,
to get to the Redeem Team,

00:07:48.667 --> 00:07:52.968
enter Coach K from Duke,
enter Jerry Colangelo.

00:07:52.968 --> 00:07:55.100
And they decided to
build a team.

00:07:55.100 --> 00:07:57.667
And, so, we spent the next
three summers in Vegas.

00:07:57.667 --> 00:07:58.868
We had a great time.

00:07:58.868 --> 00:08:01.300
-Yeah, yeah.
I could imagine, yeah.

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:03.067
-We spent the
next three summers in Vegas

00:08:03.067 --> 00:08:05.767
building, like, chemistry
and building continuity

00:08:05.767 --> 00:08:06.934
and building the team.

00:08:06.934 --> 00:08:09.634
-How was Coach K?
-Coach K is awesome.

00:08:09.634 --> 00:08:11.400
-Yeah, he's just cool, right?
-He's just cool.

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:14.667
And I didn't know he
said [bleep] so many times.

00:08:15.234 --> 00:08:17.067
Can I say that on TV?

00:08:17.067 --> 00:08:18.267
It was great.
-Yeah, it was great.

00:08:18.267 --> 00:08:19.334
-He's like, "These..."

00:08:19.334 --> 00:08:20.567
I was like, "Yes,
I'm ready to go play."

00:08:20.567 --> 00:08:21.834
-Really? Yeah.

00:08:21.834 --> 00:08:24.367
I went to go see him coach once,
and he was just yelling.

00:08:24.367 --> 00:08:25.968
He was pointing
at some clipboards like...

00:08:25.968 --> 00:08:27.467
[ Shouting indistinctly ]

00:08:27.467 --> 00:08:29.501
And they lost the game.

00:08:29.501 --> 00:08:30.734
And then, at the end, they go,
"Do we want to go back

00:08:30.734 --> 00:08:31.968
and say hi to Coach?"

00:08:31.968 --> 00:08:33.801
I go, "No. I don't ever
want to see that guy.

00:08:33.801 --> 00:08:35.501
He scares me. He frightens me."

00:08:35.501 --> 00:08:38.167
-That was him at like --
So, our games was at 9:00 p.m.

00:08:38.167 --> 00:08:40.901
We were in China in 2008.

00:08:40.901 --> 00:08:44.567
And that was him at 9:00 a.m. at
walk-through and shoot-around.

00:08:44.567 --> 00:08:47.567
He was fired up and ready to go.

00:08:47.567 --> 00:08:49.434
-Yeah. But all of you guys were.

00:08:49.434 --> 00:08:50.968
-Yeah, well,
after losing, we had --

00:08:50.968 --> 00:08:52.267
It's called the Redeem Team.

00:08:52.267 --> 00:08:54.367
We had to redeem ourselves.
-And you got the gold.

00:08:54.367 --> 00:08:55.667
-Yeah, we got the gold.
-That's the way to do it.

00:08:55.667 --> 00:08:57.467
Gold medal.
-Yes, sir.

00:08:57.467 --> 00:08:59.334
-And it's fun to have
the bronze, too.

00:08:59.334 --> 00:09:01.868
-Yeah. So, I thought --
We thought it was a great time

00:09:01.868 --> 00:09:04.434
to be able to tell this story.

00:09:04.434 --> 00:09:07.367
Obviously, our brother,
"Kob," is not here,

00:09:07.367 --> 00:09:11.000
but to have his presence and his
voice in this documentary,

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:12.868
to have "Bron's" presence
and "Melo's" presence

00:09:12.868 --> 00:09:16.501
and Coach K, like, all
the voices to tell this story.

00:09:16.501 --> 00:09:18.701
And this was pre-Instagram.

00:09:18.701 --> 00:09:21.133
This was right when Twitter
probably popped off.

00:09:21.133 --> 00:09:24.234
No one really knows about
the Redeem Team and, you know,

00:09:24.234 --> 00:09:27.100
what all came about
to get to that place.

00:09:27.100 --> 00:09:29.167
So I think they're
going to be surprised,

00:09:29.167 --> 00:09:30.868
and it's a
pretty good documentary.

00:09:30.868 --> 00:09:32.300
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:34.200
Here is a clip from
"The Redeem Team."

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:35.467
Take a look.

00:09:35.467 --> 00:09:39.801
-Well, first half was disjointed
because of foul trouble.

00:09:39.801 --> 00:09:41.634
Now there were more minutes,

00:09:41.634 --> 00:09:45.667
and people were
playing different roles.

00:09:45.667 --> 00:09:48.601
-They bring in Dwyane Wade
and Deron Williams

00:09:48.601 --> 00:09:50.200
a little earlier than expected.

00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:52.267
-Sometimes, you feel like
you've been there before,

00:09:52.267 --> 00:09:53.400
you've done this before.

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:54.901
Like, I knew I was
going to have a big game.

00:09:54.901 --> 00:09:56.367
And when I got in,
I got right to it.

00:09:56.367 --> 00:09:59.167
-Wade to the basket.
Goes inside.

00:09:59.167 --> 00:10:01.501
Beautiful move.

00:10:01.501 --> 00:10:04.067
There's Wade with the steal.

00:10:06.367 --> 00:10:09.901
-Not only did I get two fouls
early, Kobe did, too.

00:10:09.901 --> 00:10:11.767
And that set the stage
for D-Wade.

00:10:11.767 --> 00:10:13.934
-Yeah, come on!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:13.934 --> 00:10:15.734
That's the way you do it
right there.

00:10:15.734 --> 00:10:18.167
Dwyane Wade, everybody!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:18.167 --> 00:10:21.834
"The Redeem Team" begins
streaming on Netflix tomorrow.

00:10:21.834 --> 00:10:23.334
We'll be right back with
a performance from

00:10:23.334 --> 00:10:24.968
Quavo and Takeoff.

00:10:24.968 --> 00:10:25.968
Stick around, everybody.

